    },
    {
      "id": "NJgmrvJQx--_02YClgpqq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 549.7825608159989,
      "y": -290.64423893838034,
      "width": 840.7593994140625,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1937533049,
      "version": 3276,
      "versionNonce": 2126899644,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1743103357912,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Responsibilities \n- maintain overall state of stream.\n- consume -> update state -> flush to persist\n ( this depends on the read query pattern )\n- state consistency -> atomic , lock etc.\n- reliability -> flush + maintain secondary\n  backup node, replay ( event sourcing ) retention in kafka.\n ( *make sure about retry queue removal and maintain order etc. )\n- recovery -> at time of starting node from persist.\n...................................................................................................\n- scale: ( oops complex man ) -> same like if possible to distribute by some\n  do that like in case of stock could be with stock name. (google, amazon)\n  but not for top k. ( or what if particular stock have high -> go one level and\n  again try to partition -> like may be a/c to price, timing )\n- separate read and write , read eventual, write concrete. \n- multiple nodes , there separate generated results. ( master-master ) , \n  now , and shared with multiple nodes. ( quorum ), but possible only if\n  separated result could be merged -> would require raft algo.(master-master, any one \n  can read and write ) (all these are readymate by different tools. this might \n  be doing like local and then merging etc not sure.  )\n............................................................\n- famous usecase already have things in market: flink, spark\n  hadoop etc. distributed system with these gaurantees.\n \n  \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Responsibilities \n- maintain overall state of stream.\n- consume -> update state -> flush to persist\n ( this depends on the read query pattern )\n- state consistency -> atomic , lock etc.\n- reliability -> flush + maintain secondary\n  backup node, replay ( event sourcing ) retention in kafka.\n ( *make sure about retry queue removal and maintain order etc. )\n- recovery -> at time of starting node from persist.\n...................................................................................................\n- scale: ( oops complex man ) -> same like if possible to distribute by some\n  do that like in case of stock could be with stock name. (google, amazon)\n  but not for top k. ( or what if particular stock have high -> go one level and\n  again try to partition -> like may be a/c to price, timing )\n- separate read and write , read eventual, write concrete. \n- multiple nodes , there separate generated results. ( master-master ) , \n  now , and shared with multiple nodes. ( quorum ), but possible only if\n  separated result could be merged -> would require raft algo.(master-master, any one \n  can read and write ) (all these are readymate by different tools. this might \n  be doing like local and then merging etc not sure.  )\n............................................................\n- famous usecase already have things in market: flink, spark\n  hadoop etc. distributed system with these gaurantees.\n \n  \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
